(3517214, 490785, 66515, '<td valign="top">Interesting colors. The vase is a little underexposed. Darkening more would create a silhouette which would be nice. A little lighter and it would show more detail. I would move the horizon line up so that it is above the flowers and vase. The way it is now it "cuts" the vase. <br/> <br/>The pronounced shadow is a nice touch. <br/> <br/>The composition works well. <br/> <br/>A shallower depth of field would help make the background more effective. <br/> <br/>The challenge: <br/>Not really contr-jour. The shadow is falling to the right which means that the main source of light (the sun) is to the left. (Out of the frame). Now if the shadow was to fall towards you...</td>', 'Interesting colors. The vase is a little underexposed. Darkening more would create a silhouette which would be nice. A little lighter and it would show more detail. I would move the horizon line up so that it is above the flowers and vase. The way it is now it "cuts" the vase.  The pronounced shadow is a nice touch.  The composition works well.  A shallower depth of field would help make the background more effective.  The challenge: Not really contr-jour. The shadow is falling to the right which means that the main source of light (the sun) is to the left. (Out of the frame). Now if the shadow was to fall towards you...', '2007-04-04 02:48:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(3517215, 490543, 66515, '<td valign="top">This does meet the challenge but the sun creates a really big blown highlight which is really distracting. Getting  behind the tree to "cover" the sun would have helped.</td>', 'This does meet the challenge but the sun creates a really big blown highlight which is really distracting. Getting  behind the tree to "cover" the sun would have helped.', '2007-04-04 02:49:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(3517216, 490253, 66515, '<td valign="top">Nice silhouette. Remember in basic you are allowed to clone out sensor dust. Other than that this is a nice picture which has good detail.</td>', 'Nice silhouette. Remember in basic you are allowed to clone out sensor dust. Other than that this is a nice picture which has good detail.', '2007-04-04 02:49:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(3517224, 492591, 6804, '<td valign="top">Perfect in every way!!!  What a find.  This is my highest rated shot of the challenge and a new favorite!  10+</td>', 'Perfect in every way!!!  What a find.  This is my highest rated shot of the challenge and a new favorite!  10+', '2007-04-04 02:52:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3517226, 491844, 66515, '<td valign="top">The subject appears to be the flag however it gets lost in the trees in the background.  Not sure how to get this so it still meets the challenge and avoid getting the trees in the background.</td>', 'The subject appears to be the flag however it gets lost in the trees in the background.  Not sure how to get this so it still meets the challenge and avoid getting the trees in the background.', '2007-04-04 02:52:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(3517231, 492666, 66515, '<td valign="top">A smaller border would be nice here. The thick border is somewhat distracting. <br/> <br/>The composition works well and draws your eye to the sun as the focal point.</td>', 'A smaller border would be nice here. The thick border is somewhat distracting.  The composition works well and draws your eye to the sun as the focal point.', '2007-04-04 02:53:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(3517239, 492305, 66515, '<td valign="top">Interesting approach to the challenge. (Which did you use by the way?). This could use a bit of straightening but nothing major. <br/> <br/>Something about the composition is a little "off". Part of me wants to get rid of some of the stairs however I like the play of shadows/light on them. I guess its the dark area around the lamp that is the problem for me.<br/> <br/>Well done in any event.</td>', 'Interesting approach to the challenge. (Which did you use by the way?). This could use a bit of straightening but nothing major.  Something about the composition is a little "off". Part of me wants to get rid of some of the stairs however I like the play of shadows/light on them. I guess its the dark area around the lamp that is the problem for me. Well done in any event.', '2007-04-04 02:56:53.000000', NULL, 1),
