(3522401, 491166, 30049, '<td valign="top">As a stand alone photo it''s "ok" IMO.  I like the way the shoreline mimics the curving lines of the clouds.  This effect helps to offset the feeling of a centered composition some.  As is, this image still has some strong central themes to it with the horizon bisecting the photo pretty much in half.  Not being there personally I can''t say whether or not I would have taken the same image, or moved in some manner to offset the sun and horizon.<br/> <br/>Regarding the challenge theme - not too sure this is in the spirit of the challenge.  Technically, I guess it fits since you are shooting toward the light.  If you had a subject in the foreground (other than landscape) it might feel different.<br/> <br/>Just my observations.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'As a stand alone photo it''s "ok" IMO.  I like the way the shoreline mimics the curving lines of the clouds.  This effect helps to offset the feeling of a centered composition some.  As is, this image still has some strong central themes to it with the horizon bisecting the photo pretty much in half.  Not being there personally I can''t say whether or not I would have taken the same image, or moved in some manner to offset the sun and horizon. Regarding the challenge theme - not too sure this is in the spirit of the challenge.  Technically, I guess it fits since you are shooting toward the light.  If you had a subject in the foreground (other than landscape) it might feel different. Just my observations.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-04-05 14:22:04.000000', NULL, 1),
