(3524790, 492440, 62895, '<td valign="top">I can''t wait to see how this was done. You have a good thing going here.</td>', 'I can''t wait to see how this was done. You have a good thing going here.', '2007-04-06 11:21:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(3525007, 491257, 5792, '<td valign="top">One of the most interesting and provocative submissions. Pure studio nudes wouldn''t normally come to mind as a subject for contre-jour but you pulled it off in a most fascinating and appropriate way. There probably will be a few, not many, voters that feel studio shots cannot be contre-jour but the quality of your image will carry the day. Your model is attractive, you flattered her in composition, particularly with her facial lighting. BW is good and tones are excellent. Sharpness is just right. Great job!</td>', 'One of the most interesting and provocative submissions. Pure studio nudes wouldn''t normally come to mind as a subject for contre-jour but you pulled it off in a most fascinating and appropriate way. There probably will be a few, not many, voters that feel studio shots cannot be contre-jour but the quality of your image will carry the day. Your model is attractive, you flattered her in composition, particularly with her facial lighting. BW is good and tones are excellent. Sharpness is just right. Great job!', '2007-04-06 12:51:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(3525029, 490477, 64853, '<td valign="top">Very good definition!</td>', 'Very good definition!', '2007-04-06 13:00:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3525063, 491503, 27514, '<td valign="top">would like to see things a little sharper here.</td>', 'would like to see things a little sharper here.', '2007-04-06 13:16:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(3525065, 491268, 30049, '<td valign="top">I like the idea and concept of this shot.  Not sure that you could have changed much (controlling the timing) but I think this would be stronger if the couple were more of a silhouette.  As it is the photo begs for fill light or go all the way to silhouette.  <br/> <br/>Some other compositional observations; <br/>1) A more face-to-face shot might have more impact.<br/>2) Moving the couple off-center would be more dynamic.<br/>3) A tighter or farther out framing could improve this by not having all of them, except their feet, in the photo.<br/>4) The POV presented to the viewer could be more unique, i.e. shooting up or down instead of straight on.<br/> <br/>I think this setting and your subject material has a lot of potential.  Just need to move away from a snapshot type feel to a more artistic approach IMO.<br/> <br/>All of the above is JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I like the idea and concept of this shot.  Not sure that you could have changed much (controlling the timing) but I think this would be stronger if the couple were more of a silhouette.  As it is the photo begs for fill light or go all the way to silhouette.   Some other compositional observations; 1) A more face-to-face shot might have more impact.2) Moving the couple off-center would be more dynamic.3) A tighter or farther out framing could improve this by not having all of them, except their feet, in the photo.4) The POV presented to the viewer could be more unique, i.e. shooting up or down instead of straight on. I think this setting and your subject material has a lot of potential.  Just need to move away from a snapshot type feel to a more artistic approach IMO. All of the above is JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-04-06 13:17:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(3525086, 492606, 34059, '<td valign="top">I like very much the sky in this picture, but I wish there was a more interesting subject in the foreground...</td>', 'I like very much the sky in this picture, but I wish there was a more interesting subject in the foreground...', '2007-04-06 13:24:56.000000', NULL, 1),
