(3537761, 490352, 33352, '<td valign="top">Nice strong finnish again Shez, the blue didn''t put the voters off... well done</td>', 'Nice strong finnish again Shez, the blue didn''t put the voters off... well done', '2007-04-11 03:37:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3537767, 492420, 73541, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MonicaJames:</b></div><hr/><i> There is light coming from the left that destroys the silhouette. Based on the shadows, it is either street lights or light from a building or a remote-flash firing? 6. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There was absolutely no light from the left. Trees are illuminated from the right and shadows on the street are -as well- caused by light from the right.<br/> <br/>Anyway, it wasn''t intended to produce silhouettes. They weren''t asked for. I think the picture would be (even) less attractive as pure silhouettes.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the most detailed comment I got in this challenge and points that increased my avarage ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by MonicaJames: There is light coming from the left that destroys the silhouette. Based on the shadows, it is either street lights or light from a building or a remote-flash firing? 6.   There was absolutely no light from the left. Trees are illuminated from the right and shadows on the street are -as well- caused by light from the right. Anyway, it wasn''t intended to produce silhouettes. They weren''t asked for. I think the picture would be (even) less attractive as pure silhouettes. Thanks for the most detailed comment I got in this challenge and points that increased my avarage ;-)', '2007-04-11 03:41:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3537770, 492449, 33352, '<td valign="top">Very nice finnish Deb, way to go.</td>', 'Very nice finnish Deb, way to go.', '2007-04-11 03:41:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3537771, 490270, 19831, '<td valign="top">Well, it fits the challenge. I agree, it is not a technically bad shot at all. The subject is alright, not real exciting, but not boring at all either. The lamppost, I don''t see it as any kind of major distraction. I don''t think it really takes anything <i>away</i> from the image, but at the same time, it feels a little out of place, and I can''t help but think maybe the shot would have a miniscule bit more impact without it, if that makes any sense :-) One could wonder about the centered comp, but I think in this case it works alright, maybe getting out of the center would be good, but maybe not, you''d have to explore that. So there are possibly things that could be done different, like composition, fill light, etc, but who knows if it would make a difference? As far as the lack of comments, I think you''ve just landed in a comment no-man''s land. There are no glaring flaws to point out. It is not totally lacking interest or boring. It is not a dnmc. But there is not anything outstanding present. Nothing to really move a viewer, or connect with or engage with them. In other words my friend...You are missing that ever elusive and highly un-definable ''Wow factor''. :-)</td>', 'Well, it fits the challenge. I agree, it is not a technically bad shot at all. The subject is alright, not real exciting, but not boring at all either. The lamppost, I don''t see it as any kind of major distraction. I don''t think it really takes anything away from the image, but at the same time, it feels a little out of place, and I can''t help but think maybe the shot would have a miniscule bit more impact without it, if that makes any sense :-) One could wonder about the centered comp, but I think in this case it works alright, maybe getting out of the center would be good, but maybe not, you''d have to explore that. So there are possibly things that could be done different, like composition, fill light, etc, but who knows if it would make a difference? As far as the lack of comments, I think you''ve just landed in a comment no-man''s land. There are no glaring flaws to point out. It is not totally lacking interest or boring. It is not a dnmc. But there is not anything outstanding present. Nothing to really move a viewer, or connect with or engage with them. In other words my friend...You are missing that ever elusive and highly un-definable ''Wow factor''. :-)', '2007-04-11 03:42:22.000000', NULL, 0),
