(3539668, 491083, 40718, '<td valign="top">Most excellent blue.  The Contre-jour is great.  It wasa the subject matter that limited the piece.  There is a lack of "wow" or emotional engagement that makes people stop and look.  They see the shot for 2-3 seconds (literally), vote 5-6 because it''s technically good, and move on.  The 8-10 votes come when people stop and stare because they are sucked in to what they see.</td>', 'Most excellent blue.  The Contre-jour is great.  It wasa the subject matter that limited the piece.  There is a lack of "wow" or emotional engagement that makes people stop and look.  They see the shot for 2-3 seconds (literally), vote 5-6 because it''s technically good, and move on.  The 8-10 votes come when people stop and stare because they are sucked in to what they see.', '2007-04-11 14:06:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3539669, 491508, 60846, '<td valign="top">wow. this is so good. great job! congrats!</td>', 'wow. this is so good. great job! congrats!', '2007-04-11 14:06:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3539684, 491082, 66201, '<td valign="top">I can only offer you my personal response (which is not at all in line with general DPC voters so take it with a pinch of salt)... plants as such lack drama. I gave you a 5 in voting it seems.... I think with a big challenge where the voter is flipping through 329 images, the ones that meet the challenge adequately, kind of fall into the 5 zone. If they have a certain amount of drama/interest they move up into the 6''s. Excellent technicals and "story" end up in the 7''s...Looking at your score spread, you got a few 9''s and 7''s which is great. Can''t account for the dweebs that gave you 2''s, 3''s and 4''s... <br/> <br/>The very centre of the sun is very blown out and harsh on the eye. It''s a pretty enough image and fits the criteria, but that''s sort of where it ends...it''s not saying anything special and it has that technical fault. Hope that helps and doesn''t hurt too much :-(</td>', 'I can only offer you my personal response (which is not at all in line with general DPC voters so take it with a pinch of salt)... plants as such lack drama. I gave you a 5 in voting it seems.... I think with a big challenge where the voter is flipping through 329 images, the ones that meet the challenge adequately, kind of fall into the 5 zone. If they have a certain amount of drama/interest they move up into the 6''s. Excellent technicals and "story" end up in the 7''s...Looking at your score spread, you got a few 9''s and 7''s which is great. Can''t account for the dweebs that gave you 2''s, 3''s and 4''s...  The very centre of the sun is very blown out and harsh on the eye. It''s a pretty enough image and fits the criteria, but that''s sort of where it ends...it''s not saying anything special and it has that technical fault. Hope that helps and doesn''t hurt too much :-(', '2007-04-11 14:11:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3539722, 492440, 70369, '<td valign="top">Those who doubt should thank you for the lesson they learned !!! I think anyone who bases their vote on wether or not they think a shot meets the editing rules should be ashamed.. :-) One great lesson I have learned on here is to vote and "hope" it falls within the rules.. It never ceases to amaze me how creative &amp; talented people are with lighting &amp; the use of their camera.. You''ve proven that here. Great job and I would love to see your "edited" version of this so you can have a chance to fix any flaws you see.. Great job !!!</td>', 'Those who doubt should thank you for the lesson they learned !!! I think anyone who bases their vote on wether or not they think a shot meets the editing rules should be ashamed.. :-) One great lesson I have learned on here is to vote and "hope" it falls within the rules.. It never ceases to amaze me how creative & talented people are with lighting & the use of their camera.. You''ve proven that here. Great job and I would love to see your "edited" version of this so you can have a chance to fix any flaws you see.. Great job !!!', '2007-04-11 14:21:44.000000', NULL, 0),
