(3540416, 492718, 73575, '<td valign="top">Very nice; I think this would look great cropped down; the guy just doesn''t mesh with the rest of the picture (as already stated). Hope you don''t mind, but I took the liberty of playing with this, for less than 1 minute actually; just cropped both sides to center.<br/> <br/><a href="//homerbob.8m.com/pix/cropped.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"> <br/>//homerbob.8m.com/pix/cropped.jpg</a> (Sorry no thumb; my website doesn''t allow remote linking to images)<br/> <br/>(Hope this doesn''t offend you; will remove on request)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-04-11 17:31:26.</i></td>', 'Very nice; I think this would look great cropped down; the guy just doesn''t mesh with the rest of the picture (as already stated). Hope you don''t mind, but I took the liberty of playing with this, for less than 1 minute actually; just cropped both sides to center.  //homerbob.8m.com/pix/cropped.jpg (Sorry no thumb; my website doesn''t allow remote linking to images) (Hope this doesn''t offend you; will remove on request)', '2007-04-11 18:23:42.000000', '2007-04-11 18:31:26.000000', 0),
(3540463, 492449, 15711, '<td valign="top">90th??  What a joke.  I''m just not understanding.  I love the subtlety of this.  GREAT artful shot, Deb.</td>', '90th??  What a joke.  I''m just not understanding.  I love the subtlety of this.  GREAT artful shot, Deb.', '2007-04-11 18:37:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540486, 492446, 66384, '<td valign="top">I agree with Boyd -- this is creepy. Interesting, because it is usually the night shots of cemeteries that are creepy, while the day shots are usually peaceful. The contre-jour seems to have the effect of bringing the night feel to the day photo.</td>', 'I agree with Boyd -- this is creepy. Interesting, because it is usually the night shots of cemeteries that are creepy, while the day shots are usually peaceful. The contre-jour seems to have the effect of bringing the night feel to the day photo.', '2007-04-11 18:43:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540519, 492668, 66384, '<td valign="top">I feel like I''m looking through dirty eyeglasses when I look at this shot. Even though I like the patterns on the snow, I can''t get beyond the ill effect of the lens flare.</td>', 'I feel like I''m looking through dirty eyeglasses when I look at this shot. Even though I like the patterns on the snow, I can''t get beyond the ill effect of the lens flare.', '2007-04-11 18:51:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540566, 491013, 66384, '<td valign="top">When I first looked at this in our TS results posting, I though, "Do we have a new member named Icarus?" That would be a cool userid.<br/> <br/>Anyway, about the photo -- I gave it an 8 because I like it a lot! It has an Easter feel about it with the flare of the sun and the cross effect of the outlet and horizon. I like the way the sunlight seems to flow out with the water. Sorry, I should have gone even higher on the score.</td>', 'When I first looked at this in our TS results posting, I though, "Do we have a new member named Icarus?" That would be a cool userid. Anyway, about the photo -- I gave it an 8 because I like it a lot! It has an Easter feel about it with the flare of the sun and the cross effect of the outlet and horizon. I like the way the sunlight seems to flow out with the water. Sorry, I should have gone even higher on the score.', '2007-04-11 19:02:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540662, 490497, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Nuzzer,<br/> <br/>         Love the compostion, two leeding lines work wonderful the bush &amp; the grass very nice touch. Like the placement of the tree clearly giving scale to the entire image. Don''t think you got up to late either, the fog is just right thick enough to see clearly yet thin enough to peer through very well done. The only thing here that needs addressing is he hot spot (sun)  polerizing filter may have toned down the glare &amp; given you a deeper blue sky. With that being said, this is a wonderful image. Great framing, nice colors, &amp; a stunning visual effect, A truly stunning image....Great job.<br/> <br/>Frankie/Las Vegas</td>', 'Hi Nuzzer,          Love the compostion, two leeding lines work wonderful the bush & the grass very nice touch. Like the placement of the tree clearly giving scale to the entire image. Don''t think you got up to late either, the fog is just right thick enough to see clearly yet thin enough to peer through very well done. The only thing here that needs addressing is he hot spot (sun)  polerizing filter may have toned down the glare & given you a deeper blue sky. With that being said, this is a wonderful image. Great framing, nice colors, & a stunning visual effect, A truly stunning image....Great job. Frankie/Las Vegas', '2007-04-11 19:42:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540691, 490934, 66384, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bmartuch:</b></div><hr/><i> Julianne, I think this is a great shot but it doesn''t seem to have back lighting. You should have entered this in FS. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hmmm... his back looks lit to me. :P <br/> <br/>Just kidding. I knew this was stretching the bounds of contre-jour, but it was the best I had at the time.</td>', 'Originally posted by bmartuch: Julianne, I think this is a great shot but it doesn''t seem to have back lighting. You should have entered this in FS.  Hmmm... his back looks lit to me. :P  Just kidding. I knew this was stretching the bounds of contre-jour, but it was the best I had at the time.', '2007-04-11 20:02:43.000000', NULL, 0),
