(3540770, 491532, 66384, '<td valign="top">I think this is a very uplifting and pretty image. Truly representative of Spring. To me it represents good things, and the promise of many good things yet to come.</td>', 'I think this is a very uplifting and pretty image. Truly representative of Spring. To me it represents good things, and the promise of many good things yet to come.', '2007-04-11 20:29:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540779, 490644, 66597, '<td valign="top">Welcome to DPC, great start! You picked a tough challenge to cut your teeth on :-) I notice your question about getting rid of the pink (sun flare). In basic editing, you can''t clone anything out, so you chose right to keep it there. In advanced editing, it would be your artistic choice.</td>', 'Welcome to DPC, great start! You picked a tough challenge to cut your teeth on :-) I notice your question about getting rid of the pink (sun flare). In basic editing, you can''t clone anything out, so you chose right to keep it there. In advanced editing, it would be your artistic choice.', '2007-04-11 20:32:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540827, 490555, 66384, '<td valign="top">This is lovely and charming. A great capture. The light is beautiful, and I think the saturation is just right. The only criticism I have is that it may be a tad over-sharpened.</td>', 'This is lovely and charming. A great capture. The light is beautiful, and I think the saturation is just right. The only criticism I have is that it may be a tad over-sharpened.', '2007-04-11 20:43:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540847, 490495, 66384, '<td valign="top">Love the flare of the sun. I gave this a 9.</td>', 'Love the flare of the sun. I gave this a 9.', '2007-04-11 20:50:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540919, 490950, 66952, '<td valign="top">I saw your forum post...I''ll bite...<br/> <br/>The image definitely meets the challenge, and you''ve done a nice job keeping the sky blue behind the tree and sun, which is often harder than it looks. The trouble with shooting straight into the sun is that the sun is a really bright light, and everything that isn''t the sun becomes unnaturally dark. It looks like you''re trying to show the sunlight filtering through the fuzzy seed things, but the sun''s really bright, so there''s too much contrast for it to be attractive. You might try shooting when the sun''s lower in the sky and not so bright. <br/> <br/>The other thing is to be careful of your background. In this shot, there''s some black, blobby looking pine trees in the background. In the lower right corner, they serve a purpose of showing off the sunlight on the birch tree, but on the left side, they''re just dark and distracting, and they look like they''re leaning backwards, because the camera is pointed towards the sky.<br/> <br/>I think on a shot like this, it really helps to ask yourself 2 questions:<br/> <br/>1) What is the subject?<br/>2) Is there anything in the shot that''s going to pull the viewer''s focus away from the subject?<br/> <br/>I just looked at your portfolio. It''s no accident that on your top rated images, you''ve done a great job of isolating the subject, and on the lower rated images, you haven''t. Especially on DPC, when the voters only look at the image for a few seconds, if there''s anything distracting, the voter won''t take the time to look any further.<br/></td>', 'I saw your forum post...I''ll bite... The image definitely meets the challenge, and you''ve done a nice job keeping the sky blue behind the tree and sun, which is often harder than it looks. The trouble with shooting straight into the sun is that the sun is a really bright light, and everything that isn''t the sun becomes unnaturally dark. It looks like you''re trying to show the sunlight filtering through the fuzzy seed things, but the sun''s really bright, so there''s too much contrast for it to be attractive. You might try shooting when the sun''s lower in the sky and not so bright.  The other thing is to be careful of your background. In this shot, there''s some black, blobby looking pine trees in the background. In the lower right corner, they serve a purpose of showing off the sunlight on the birch tree, but on the left side, they''re just dark and distracting, and they look like they''re leaning backwards, because the camera is pointed towards the sky. I think on a shot like this, it really helps to ask yourself 2 questions: 1) What is the subject?2) Is there anything in the shot that''s going to pull the viewer''s focus away from the subject? I just looked at your portfolio. It''s no accident that on your top rated images, you''ve done a great job of isolating the subject, and on the lower rated images, you haven''t. Especially on DPC, when the voters only look at the image for a few seconds, if there''s anything distracting, the voter won''t take the time to look any further.', '2007-04-11 21:14:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540951, 490843, 46177, '<td valign="top">Nice colours and I really like the angle you took this at, very dramatic shot.</td>', 'Nice colours and I really like the angle you took this at, very dramatic shot.', '2007-04-11 21:23:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540965, 490950, 7743, '<td valign="top">I like your idea.  The highlights of the tree with the sun behind can make for an amazing image.<br/> <br/>In this case though I think the sun is a bit too central and not enough of the tree (IMO) is getting benefit from the back lighting.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I like your idea.  The highlights of the tree with the sun behind can make for an amazing image. In this case though I think the sun is a bit too central and not enough of the tree (IMO) is getting benefit from the back lighting. ', '2007-04-11 21:26:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3540995, 491508, 64009, '<td valign="top">Dudski, one of the most creative pictures I have seen for a long time now here at dpchallenge. Congrats !!</td>', 'Dudski, one of the most creative pictures I have seen for a long time now here at dpchallenge. Congrats !!', '2007-04-11 21:33:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3541048, 491605, 22301, '<td valign="top">This is really cool use of the challenge, by using a long line of light under the pier as opposed to just the sun that gives the classic circular glow. this may have also been a reason why it didn''t score so well, as it wouldn''t be what the normal voter had in mind. I think it is cool, i would have like to have seen the light coming a little lower in the frame, so the light doesn''t pop out of the top of her head. Other than that it is really creative entry, IMO.</td>', 'This is really cool use of the challenge, by using a long line of light under the pier as opposed to just the sun that gives the classic circular glow. this may have also been a reason why it didn''t score so well, as it wouldn''t be what the normal voter had in mind. I think it is cool, i would have like to have seen the light coming a little lower in the frame, so the light doesn''t pop out of the top of her head. Other than that it is really creative entry, IMO.', '2007-04-11 21:46:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3541066, 491508, 46177, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your blue ribbon.  This is a very beautiful image and well deserving of your great score!</td>', 'Congratulations on your blue ribbon.  This is a very beautiful image and well deserving of your great score!', '2007-04-11 21:51:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3541067, 491471, 46177, '<td valign="top">A stunning shot that really stands out, congratulations on your ribbon.</td>', 'A stunning shot that really stands out, congratulations on your ribbon.', '2007-04-11 21:51:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3541069, 490497, 46177, '<td valign="top">Absolutely lovely, congratulations on your ribbon.</td>', 'Absolutely lovely, congratulations on your ribbon.', '2007-04-11 21:52:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3541099, 492690, 1717, '<td valign="top">stop beating me! :-P <br/> <br/>you''re getting a lot of use out of that fog machine.  money well spent, eh?  really a great shot! :)</td>', 'stop beating me! :-P  you''re getting a lot of use out of that fog machine.  money well spent, eh?  really a great shot! :)', '2007-04-11 22:01:36.000000', NULL, 0),
