(3542322, 492265, 76798, '<td valign="top">I like how you''ve taken a scene which I would not have normally considere "pretty" and portrayed it so artistically.  Kudos.</td>', 'I like how you''ve taken a scene which I would not have normally considere "pretty" and portrayed it so artistically.  Kudos.', '2007-04-12 10:20:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3542486, 491634, 31403, '<td valign="top">this is a great idea - I may have to try it!  The crazy card game of choice at our house is "hand and foot".  I''d rather take photos, but the rest LOVE it!<br/> <br/>I''m thinking a tripod will go a long way to helping with my shot, or maybe just setting the camera on the table.  I want the hands moving and the person rocking a little, but the table and the cards not being touched and the background to be in focus - so the people are moving but some stuff isn''t.<br/> <br/>See what ideas you gave me?<br/> <br/>I''m not saying YOU should do that - because you are developing a very unique style - you''ll laugh when you hang your own show, or shoot for an ad agency with your style while the rest of DPC is still here giving each other 1s.  :-)</td>', 'this is a great idea - I may have to try it!  The crazy card game of choice at our house is "hand and foot".  I''d rather take photos, but the rest LOVE it! I''m thinking a tripod will go a long way to helping with my shot, or maybe just setting the camera on the table.  I want the hands moving and the person rocking a little, but the table and the cards not being touched and the background to be in focus - so the people are moving but some stuff isn''t. See what ideas you gave me? I''m not saying YOU should do that - because you are developing a very unique style - you''ll laugh when you hang your own show, or shoot for an ad agency with your style while the rest of DPC is still here giving each other 1s.  :-)', '2007-04-12 11:10:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3542709, 492718, 43156, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by homerbob:</b></div><hr/><i> (Hope this doesn''t offend you; will remove on request) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>This doesnt offend me at all. I appreciate your time and effort trying to make my picture look better and thank you for that.<br/> <br/>Now I should tell you that this shot is pure candid, so I didnt have too many choices. I played with image quite a bit before submitting it. I tried different crops as well. Finally I submitted the one with two people for two reasons:<br/>1) It tells the story.<br/>2) From my experience with DPC I know that very thin photos dont score very well on challenges. <br/> <br/>Valeriy.</td>', 'Originally posted by homerbob: (Hope this doesn''t offend you; will remove on request)  This doesnt offend me at all. I appreciate your time and effort trying to make my picture look better and thank you for that. Now I should tell you that this shot is pure candid, so I didnt have too many choices. I played with image quite a bit before submitting it. I tried different crops as well. Finally I submitted the one with two people for two reasons:1) It tells the story.2) From my experience with DPC I know that very thin photos dont score very well on challenges.  Valeriy.', '2007-04-12 12:08:51.000000', NULL, 0),
